    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "Among <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, the total number of species having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised central atom is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridisation and bent shape containing two bond pairs and two lone pairs.&nbsp;Structure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow></msup></math> is&nbsp;tetrahedral structure and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Si</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridised.&nbsp;The molecular geometry of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is trigonal pyramidal and its electron geometry is tetrahedral. In this molecule sulphur undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hbridisation,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/448b6a2a-1994-4fdc-947f-390becd924e1.png\" style=\"width: 617px; height: 176px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/15a67b58-4f07-4be3-bb4a-0fdf2a9b80e2.png\" style=\"width: 309px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> molecule is linear molecule but it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> hybridised. In&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, sulphur undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridisation and molecule has see-saw shape. In&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, chlorine undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridisation and shape of the molecule is T-shape.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/2e238f8d-8dfd-47e2-962a-5928b8e9c844.png\" style=\"width: 596px; height: 156px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c7ab8240-d29f-46e8-8745-e2613b5dd0b7.png\" style=\"width: 257px; height: 158px;\" /></p><p>The nickel tetracarbonyl is a tetrahedral complex in which nickel metal undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation. In the molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math>&nbsp;undergo&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;hybridisation and molecular shape is see-saw. Tetrachloroplatinate(II) is a square planar complex in which platinum undergoes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hbridisation.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b40c9dc7-9e03-48c9-984e-1a11c3761abe.png\" style=\"width: 305px; height: 166px;\" /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/c5586d5e-e6a9-4231-a3d0-e1a8223bb9e0.png\" style=\"width: 628px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is square planar compound in which xenon undergoes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation. In the tetrahedral molecule&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, sulphur undergoes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3c0f7a1e-1ced-4c26-88b2-c148c5d73185.png\" style=\"width: 499px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>Hence, the total number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised central atom molecules are 5.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
